IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-interpretation`
IMPORT `g4-nouns`

-- g4-art11-application.l4: Article 11 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, paragraphs (1) to (3), (8), (10) and (11): the right to apply, what the application must include, the
-- powers of the States and of the Minister over applications, and the pass-through to the JFSC. Paragraphs (4) to (7) and (9), the Commissioner's decision, are in g4-art11-decision.l4.
-- Time. Part 4 (Articles 8 to 17) came into force on 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018); whether it is in force on a day is the integrator's wrapper, not a gate here (PLAN section 10). No entry in the Table of Endnote References
-- amends Articles 11 or 12, so one text of them is encoded for every vintage; only the identity of "the Minister" (Article 1) varies by vintage, and the rules here are typed by the ROLE `the Minister`.
-- Conventions of this module (the same in the other modules of group G4):
--   * a discretion ("in the opinion of the Commissioner", "appearing to the Minister") is an INPUT named for what it decides; nothing here computes one;
--   * a duty, power or prohibition is a regulative rule typed by the ROLE that acts and the ACT done (PARTY, MUST, MAY, SHANT); where the Law states no time, the rule has no WITHIN;
--   * a rule that is guarded by a condition answers FULFILLED when the condition fails, which means "nothing is owed or permitted here";
--   * the content of every Order and of every set of Regulations is an input: none is among the sources;
--   * a period is counted by a reading of the Interpretation record (forks F4.1, F4.2, F4.6, F4.9, F4.11); each reading is its own function, named for the fork and the reading.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `Article 11 -- Application to register`

§§§ `Article 11(1) -- the right to apply`

-- src:299 | (1) An entity (“the applicant”), that wishes to have available to it the advantages of registration as a charity under this Law, may apply to be registered.
@ref Article 11(1) (src:299)
DECIDE `the entity applies` IS `Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `apply to be registered`

-- src:299 | (1) An entity (“the applicant”), that wishes to have available to it the advantages of registration as a charity under this Law, may apply to be registered.
@ref Article 11(1) (src:299)
@export Whether an entity that wishes to have the advantages of registration as a charity may apply to be registered (Article 11(1)); answers FULFILLED where the entity is not an entity within Article 2(1) or does not wish to
GIVEN
  `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The applicant as Article 2 leaves it: its kinds of entity, whether it is a Jersey entity, its governors and its purposes
  `the entity wishes to have available to it the advantages of registration as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity wishes to have the advantages of registration under this Law
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(1) the entity may apply` IS
    IF     NOT null (`the entity`'s `kinds of entity`)
       AND `the entity wishes to have available to it the advantages of registration as a charity`
    THEN PARTY `an applicant for registration`
         MAY `the entity applies`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 11(2) -- what the applicant must provide`

-- src:300 | (2) The applicant must provide to the Commissioner, in such form as the Commissioner may publish in relation to an entity of a description into which that charity falls –
@ref Article 11(2) (src:300)
DECIDE `the applicant provides what Article 11(2) requires` IS `Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide the Commissioner with what Article 11(2) requires`

-- src:300 | (2) The applicant must provide to the Commissioner, in such form as the Commissioner may publish in relation to an entity of a description into which that charity falls –
@ref Article 11(2) (src:300)
-- The Law gives no time for providing the items, so the duty has no WITHIN; whether the application includes them is the predicate `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` below.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(2) the applicant must provide what Article 11(2) requires` IS
    PARTY `an applicant for registration`
    MUST `the applicant provides what Article 11(2) requires`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- An Order under Article 11(8)(b) may disapply a provision of paragraph (2) for a described applicant, and may modify it. That a provision is disapplied for THIS applicant is a fact the caller supplies
-- (`provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant`); that it is applied subject to a modification is absorbed in what the applicant is recorded as having provided.
-- src:341 | (b) after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities, provide that any provision of paragraph (2) –
-- src:342 | (i) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of applicants of that description, or
-- src:343 | (ii) applies to a prescribed description of applicant only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of applicants of that description.
@ref Article 11(8)(b) (src:341-343)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item of Article 11(2)` @desc The provision of Article 11(2) in question
      `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application, with the provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order under Article 11(8)(b) disapplies for this applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` IF
    NOT elem item (`the application`'s `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant`)

-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
-- src:302 | (i) how the entity meets the requirements of paragraphs (4)(c) and (d),
@ref Article 11(2)(a)(i) (src:301-302)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `information and evidence on how the entity meets the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) and (d)` `the application`
    OR  `Art 11(2)(a) the information on a matter is provided` (`the application`'s `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`'s `how the applicant meets Article 11(4)(c) and (d)`)

-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
-- src:303 | (ii) the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (d) of Article 8(3), and
@ref Article 11(2)(a)(ii) (src:301) (src:303)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(a)(ii) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `information and evidence on the matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)` `the application`
    OR  `Art 11(2)(a) the information on a matter is provided` (`the application`'s `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`'s `matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)`)

-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
-- src:304 | (iii) if applicable, the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (h), (i), (m) and (n) of Article 8(3);
@ref Article 11(2)(a)(iii) (src:301) (src:304)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `information and evidence on the matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)` `the application`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`'s `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant`
    OR  `Art 11(2)(a) the information on a matter is provided` (`the application`'s `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`'s `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)`)

-- (a): "as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered": what is provided as at the application, and, if the position once registered would differ, what is proposed.
-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
@ref Article 11(2)(a) (src:301)
GIVEN info IS AN `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` @desc The information and evidence on one of the three matters of paragraph (a)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(a) the information on a matter is provided` IF
        info's `provided as at the time of the application`
    AND (   NOT info's `would differ once the entity is registered`
         OR info's `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` )

-- src:305 | (b) a copy of the applicant’s constitution;
@ref Article 11(2)(b) (src:305)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a copy of the applicant's constitution` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)`'s `copy of the applicant's constitution`

-- src:306 | (c) a draft of the proposed statement of the entity’s registered charitable purposes;
@ref Article 11(2)(c) (src:306)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(c) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)`'s `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes`

-- src:307 | (d) a draft of the entity’s registered public benefit statement;
@ref Article 11(2)(d) (src:307)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(d) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a draft of the registered public benefit statement` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)`'s `draft of the registered public benefit statement`

§§§ `Article 11(2)(e) -- financial details`

-- src:308 | (e) details of –
-- src:309 | (i) the applicant’s most recent, if any, financial accounts,
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(i) (src:308-309)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `details of the applicant's most recent financial accounts` `the application`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `most recent financial accounts exist`
    OR  `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `details of the most recent financial accounts`

-- "details of any payment": a payment is disclosed when the application gives its details, that is, who was paid, when, and how much; the two facts about the payee that forks F4.11 reads are not details of the payment.
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to a governor` @desc The payment made to a governor
      disclosed IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor` @desc The payments whose details the application gives
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is among the details disclosed` IF
    any (GIVEN detail YIELD       detail's `name of the payee` EQUALS payment's `name of the payee`
                            AND detail's `date of the payment` EQUALS payment's `date of the payment`
                            AND detail's `amount paid` EQUALS payment's `amount paid`)
        disclosed

-- (e)(ii), first requirement: "details of any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application". The period is counted by forks F4.1 (which twelve months),
-- F4.2 (which day is "the application"), F4.6 (a year before 29 February); the payee by F4.11 (a governor when?). Each reading is a function below; the public functions take the Interpretation record.
-- src:308 | (e) details of –
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:308) (src:310)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
      `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application, with the payments made to governors and the payments the application discloses
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `details of payments to governors in the twelve months preceding the application` `the application`
    OR  all (GIVEN payment YIELD    NOT `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` interp `the application` payment
                                 OR `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is among the details disclosed` payment (`the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `payments to governors disclosed in the application`))
            (`the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `payments made to governors`)

-- (e)(ii), second requirement: "and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order". An applicant is not yet "the registered charity" (trap T28):
-- the standard input IP29 is read of the applicant as the registered charity it would become. The Law says 13(9)(b); IP29 names Article 13(9) as a whole; see FRAGMENT-G4.md.
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement of a draft statement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `a draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)` `the application`
    OR  NOT `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
    OR  `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)`

-- src:311 | (iii) any other financial information that would be required if the application were for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008, and
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(iii) (src:311)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(iii) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `other financial information required under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` `the application`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 would require other financial information`
    OR  `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `other financial information required under that Law`

-- src:312 | (iv) if the applicant is not requesting entry in the restricted section of the register, any further financial information prescribed by the Minister by Order; and
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(iv) (src:312)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `further financial information prescribed by Order` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `entry in the restricted section is requested`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `Order prescribes further financial information`
    OR  `the application`'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`'s `further financial information prescribed by Order`

§§§ `Article 11(2)(f) -- other information`

-- src:313 | (f) such other information, documents and evidence as may be –
-- src:314 | (i) required by Regulations under paragraph (3), or
@ref Article 11(2)(f)(i) (src:313-314)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(f)(i) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations under Article 11(3)` `the application`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`'s `Regulations under Article 11(3) require other information, documents or evidence`
    OR  `the application`'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`'s `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations`

-- src:313 | (f) such other information, documents and evidence as may be –
-- src:315 | (ii) otherwise requested by the Commissioner in order to determine the application.
@ref Article 11(2)(f)(ii) (src:313) (src:315)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(f)(ii) the requirement is met` IF
        NOT `Art 11(2) the provision applies to the applicant` `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner` `the application`
    OR  NOT `the application`'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`'s `Commissioner has requested other information, documents or evidence to determine the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`'s `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner`

§§§ `Article 11(2) -- the application as a whole`

-- src:300 | (2) The applicant must provide to the Commissioner, in such form as the Commissioner may publish in relation to an entity of a description into which that charity falls –
@ref Article 11(2) (src:300)
@export Whether the application includes everything Article 11(2) requires of the applicant, after any relief an Order under Article 11(8)(b) gives; counts the twelve months preceding the application on the reading given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9)(b) requires a registered charity to give a statement of its intentions about payments to governors; Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reads it of the applicant as it would be once registered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2) the application includes what Article 11(2) requires` IF
        `Art 11(2)(a)(i) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(a)(ii) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(a)(iii) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(b) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(c) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(d) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(e)(i) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement to disclose payments is met` interp `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the requirement of a draft statement is met` `the application` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
    AND `Art 11(2)(e)(iii) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(e)(iv) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(f)(i) the requirement is met` `the application`
    AND `Art 11(2)(f)(ii) the requirement is met` `the application`

§§§ `Article 11(2)(e)(ii), 11(8)(a)(i) -- the date of the application and the twelve months (periods P5, P6)`

-- The refusals of this module, one definition each, named for what is not covered. A refusal is returned, never stored (entry 11.8 of the phrasebook).
@ref Article 19(6) (src:496)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete` MEANS
    REFUSE "no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete"

-- F4.2: which day is "the application". One function per reading; the public function dispatches on the record.
-- src:496 | (6) An application for registration is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5).
@ref Article 19(6) (src:496)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.2 reading A: the date of the application is the day it is lodged` IS
    `the application`'s dates's `date lodged`

-- src:496 | (6) An application for registration is not complete if the entity has not complied with paragraph (5).
@ref Article 19(6) (src:496)
GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc The application
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.2 reading B: the date of the application is the day it becomes complete` IS
    CONSIDER `the application`'s dates's `date on which it became complete`
    WHEN JUST day THEN day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no date of the application exists under Article 19(6) until the application is complete`

@ref Articles 11(2)(e)(ii), 11(8)(a)(i) and 19(6) (src:310) (src:339) (src:496)
@export The date of the application, on the reading given: the day it is lodged, or the day it becomes complete (refuses on the second reading while the application is not complete)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Art 11 the date of the application` IS
    CONSIDER interp's `which day is the date of the application`
    WHEN `the day the application is lodged` THEN `F4.2 reading A: the date of the application is the day it is lodged` `the application`
    WHEN `the day the application becomes complete` THEN `F4.2 reading B: the date of the application is the day it becomes complete` `the application`

-- F4.6: a year before a date. Both readings agree except on 29 February.
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The date
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.6 reading A: a year before` IS `add years` day (0 MINUS 1)

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The date
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.6 reading B: a year before` IS Date (DATE_DAY day) (DATE_MONTH day) ((DATE_YEAR day) MINUS 1)

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  day IS A DATE @desc The date
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` IS
    CONSIDER interp's `how a year is taken back from 29 February`
    WHEN `a year before 29 February is 28 February` THEN `F4.6 reading A: a year before` day
    WHEN `a year before 29 February is 1 March` THEN `F4.6 reading B: a year before` day

-- F4.1: the twelve months. Each reading gives the first and the last day, both inclusive; the anchor is the date of the application (F4.2) and a year is taken back by F4.6.
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  anchor IS A DATE @desc The date of the application
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `F4.1 reading A: the twelve months ending on the day before the application` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` interp anchor), (anchor MINUS 1)

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  anchor IS A DATE @desc The date of the application
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `F4.1 reading B: the twelve months ending on the day of the application` IS
    `Period of days` OF ((`Art 11(2)(e)(ii) a year before` interp anchor) PLUS 1), anchor

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE @desc The date of the application
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `F4.1 reading C: the twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application` IS
    `Period of days` OF (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH anchor) ((DATE_YEAR anchor) MINUS 1)), ((Date 1 (DATE_MONTH anchor) (DATE_YEAR anchor)) MINUS 1)

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
@export The twelve months preceding the application (first and last day, both inclusive) on the reading given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` IS
    CONSIDER interp's `how the twelve months preceding the application are counted`
    WHEN `the twelve months ending on the day before the application` THEN `F4.1 reading A: the twelve months ending on the day before the application` interp (`Art 11 the date of the application` interp `the application`)
    WHEN `the twelve months ending on the day of the application` THEN `F4.1 reading B: the twelve months ending on the day of the application` interp (`Art 11 the date of the application` interp `the application`)
    WHEN `the twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application` THEN `F4.1 reading C: the twelve whole calendar months before the month of the application` (`Art 11 the date of the application` interp `the application`)

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
@export Whether a payment made on the given day falls in the twelve months preceding the application, on the reading given (Article 11(2)(e)(ii))
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `the payment date` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the payment to a governor was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` IF
        `the payment date` AT LEAST period's `first day`
    AND `the payment date` AT MOST period's `last day`
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the twelve months preceding the application` interp `the application`

-- F4.11: the payee. Reading A: a governor when the payment was made; reading B: a governor on the date of the application.
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to a governor` @desc The payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.11 reading A: the payee was a governor when the payment was made` IF
    payment's `payee was a governor when the payment was made`

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to a governor` @desc The payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `F4.11 reading B: the payee is a governor on the date of the application` IF
    payment's `payee is a governor on the date of the application`

@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
@export Whether a payment is one that Article 11(2)(e)(ii) requires the application to disclose: a payment to a governor, made in the twelve months preceding the application, on the readings given
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  payment IS A `Payment to a governor` @desc The payment, with its date and the facts about its payee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment is one the paragraph reaches` IF
        `Art 11(2)(e)(ii) the payment to a governor is within the period` interp `the application` (payment's `date of the payment`)
    AND (CONSIDER interp's `which payees Article 11(2)(e)(ii) reaches`
         WHEN `a payee who was a governor when the payment was made` THEN `F4.11 reading A: the payee was a governor when the payment was made` payment
         WHEN `a payee who is a governor on the date of the application` THEN `F4.11 reading B: the payee is a governor on the date of the application` payment)

§§§ `Article 11(3) -- Regulations on information and procedure`

-- src:316 | (3) The States may by Regulations –
-- src:317 | (a) prescribe other information, documents or evidence that must be provided on an application;
@ref Article 11(3)(a) (src:316-317)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(3)(a) the States may prescribe other information, documents or evidence` IS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the States`, `make Regulations prescribing other information, documents or evidence to be provided on an application`

-- src:316 | (3) The States may by Regulations –
-- src:318 | (b) make further provision as to the procedure for making an application.
@ref Article 11(3)(b) (src:316) (src:318)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(3)(b) the States may make further provision as to the procedure` IS
    PARTY `the States`
    MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the States`, `make Regulations making further provision as to the procedure for making an application`

§§§ `Article 11(8) -- Orders on decisions and on relief for small applicants`

-- src:337 | (8) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:338 | (a) make provision as to –
-- src:339 | (i) the period within which the Commissioner must make a decision on an application,
@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:337-339)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Minister may provide for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application` IS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order providing for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application`

-- src:337 | (8) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:338 | (a) make provision as to –
-- src:340 | (ii) the notification to applicants of decisions and of reasons for refusal;
@ref Article 11(8)(a)(ii) (src:337-338) (src:340)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(a)(ii) the Minister may provide for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal` IS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order providing for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal`

-- (b): the power is exercised "after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities". Whether the Minister consulted is a fact the caller supplies;
-- a body "appearing to the Minister to be representative" is the Minister's appearance, so whether the Minister consulted every such body is one input (vacuously TRUE where none appears).
-- src:341 | (b) after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities, provide that any provision of paragraph (2) –
@ref Article 11(8)(b) (src:341)
GIVEN `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted the Commissioner before making the Order
      `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted every body that appears to the Minister to be representative of interested entities; TRUE where no body so appears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` IF
        `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner`
    AND `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities`

-- src:341 | (b) after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities, provide that any provision of paragraph (2) –
-- src:342 | (i) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of applicants of that description, or
@ref Article 11(8)(b)(i) (src:341-342)
GIVEN `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted the Commissioner before making the Order
      `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted every body that appears to the Minister to be representative of interested entities; TRUE where no body so appears
      `it appears to the Minister that applicants of the description require relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of their small size, or lack of resources or expertise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's appearance, which is a discretion of the Minister and so an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(b)(i) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a prescribed description of applicant` IS
    IF     `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner` `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities`
       AND `it appears to the Minister that applicants of the description require relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of their small size, or lack of resources or expertise`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a described applicant`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:341 | (b) after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities, provide that any provision of paragraph (2) –
-- src:343 | (ii) applies to a prescribed description of applicant only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of applicants of that description.
@ref Article 11(8)(b)(ii) (src:341) (src:343)
GIVEN `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted the Commissioner before making the Order
      `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister consulted every body that appears to the Minister to be representative of interested entities; TRUE where no body so appears
      `it appears to the Minister that the modification gives reasonable relief from the burden of the provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of applicants of the description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's appearance, which is a discretion of the Minister and so an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(b)(ii) the Minister may provide that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a prescribed description of applicant subject to a modification` IS
    IF     `Art 11(8)(b) the Minister has consulted as the paragraph requires` `the Minister has consulted the Commissioner` `the Minister has consulted every body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested entities`
       AND `it appears to the Minister that the modification gives reasonable relief from the burden of the provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of applicants of the description`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `Act under Article 11` OF `the Minister`, `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a described applicant subject to a modification`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- P7: "the period within which the Commissioner must make a decision on an application" is fixed by an Order, and no Order is among the sources. The length is an input; when it is not supplied the model refuses
-- by name. The period is counted from the date of the application (F4.2) by F4.9: reading A starts it the day after, so the last day is the date plus the length; reading B counts that date as the first day.
-- Nothing in Article 11 says what follows if the Commissioner decides late, so no consequence of lateness is encoded.
@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:339)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixing the period for the Commissioner's decision is encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixing the period for the Commissioner's decision is encoded in this model"

@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:339)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE @desc The date of the application
      allowance IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the period in days
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.9 reading A: the last day of the period` IS anchor PLUS allowance

@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:339)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE @desc The date of the application
      allowance IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the period in days
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `F4.9 reading B: the last day of the period` IS (anchor PLUS allowance) MINUS 1

@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:339)
@export The last day on which the Commissioner may decide the application, counting the period an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes from the date of the application on the readings given; refuses where no Order's length is supplied
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `the length in days of the period that an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days the Order allows the Commissioner; NOTHING where no Order has fixed one
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` IS
    CONSIDER `the length in days of the period that an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixing the period for the Commissioner's decision is encoded in this model`
    WHEN JUST allowance THEN
        CONSIDER interp's `how the period for the Commissioner's decision is counted`
        WHEN `the period starts the day after the date of the application` THEN `F4.9 reading A: the last day of the period` (`Art 11 the date of the application` interp `the application`) allowance
        WHEN `the date of the application is the first day of the period` THEN `F4.9 reading B: the last day of the period` (`Art 11 the date of the application` interp `the application`) allowance

@ref Article 11(8)(a)(i) (src:339)
@export Whether the Commissioner decided the application within the period an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes, on the readings given; refuses where no Order's length is supplied
GIVEN
  interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12` @desc The reading of each ambiguity of Articles 11 and 12; a field left out takes the reading the encoding takes (see the fork register in FRAGMENT-G4.md)
  `the application` IS AN `Application for registration` @desc What the applicant has provided under Article 11(2), with the day it was lodged and the day, if any, it became complete
  `the length in days of the period that an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The number of days the Order allows the Commissioner; NOTHING where no Order has fixed one
  `the day of the Commissioner's decision` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Commissioner decided the application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the Commissioner's decision is within the period` IF
    `the day of the Commissioner's decision` AT MOST `Art 11(8)(a)(i) the last day for the Commissioner's decision` interp `the application` `the length in days of the period that an Order under Article 11(8)(a)(i) fixes`

§§§ `Article 11(10) and (11) -- the applicant that is also required to register under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`

-- Whether the entity "is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 but is not so registered" is a fact under a Law that is not in the sources: an input.
-- src:347 | (10) An applicant for registration, if it is an entity that is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 but is not so registered, must –
-- src:348 | (a) provide with the application any additional information that must be provided to the JFSC in an application for registration under that Law; and
@ref Article 11(10)(a) (src:347-348)
GIVEN `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is an entity that is required to be registered under that Law but is not so registered
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(10)(a) the applicant must provide the additional information with the application` IS
    IF `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not`
    THEN PARTY `an applicant for registration`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:347 | (10) An applicant for registration, if it is an entity that is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 but is not so registered, must –
-- src:349 | (b) request to be registered under that Law (by virtue of paragraph (11)).
@ref Article 11(10)(b) (src:347) (src:349)
GIVEN `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is an entity that is required to be registered under that Law but is not so registered
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(10)(b) the applicant must request to be registered under that Law` IS
    IF `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not`
    THEN PARTY `an applicant for registration`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `an applicant for registration`, `request to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:347 | (10) An applicant for registration, if it is an entity that is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 but is not so registered, must –
@ref Article 11(10) (src:347)
GIVEN `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is an entity that is required to be registered under that Law but is not so registered
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(10) the applicant must provide the additional information and request to be registered under that Law` IS
        `Art 11(10)(a) the applicant must provide the additional information with the application` `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not`
    RAND `Art 11(10)(b) the applicant must request to be registered under that Law` `the applicant is required to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 and is not`

-- src:350 | (11) If the Commissioner receives information and a request under paragraph (10) –
-- src:351 | (a) the Commissioner must pass to the JFSC that request, with the information and documents, held by the Commissioner, that must be provided to the JFSC in an application for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008; and
@ref Article 11(11)(a) (src:350-351)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has received information and a request under Article 11(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has received the information and the request that Article 11(10) requires of the applicant
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(11)(a) the Commissioner must pass the request to the JFSC` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has received information and a request under Article 11(10)`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Commissioner`, `pass the request, with the information and documents, to the JFSC`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b) is a duty of another body, the JFSC, under a Law that is not in the sources: only the duty is encoded, and it is typed by that body's role.
-- src:350 | (11) If the Commissioner receives information and a request under paragraph (10) –
-- src:352 | (b) the JFSC must treat that request, with the information and documents, as an application for registration under that Law.
@ref Article 11(11)(b) (src:350) (src:352)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has received information and a request under Article 11(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has received the information and the request that Article 11(10) requires of the applicant
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
DECIDE `Art 11(11)(b) the JFSC must treat the request as an application for registration under that Law` IS
    IF `the Commissioner has received information and a request under Article 11(10)`
    THEN PARTY `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
         MUST `Act under Article 11` OF `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`, `treat the request, with the information and documents, as an application for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
